  "solution": "Let the two roots be \\(r\\) and \\(s\\).\n\nFor the quadratic \\(3x^2+4x-9=0\\), Vieta’s formulas give:\n\n\\[\nr+s=-\\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nrs=\\frac{-9}{3}=-3\n\\]\n\nWe want the sum of the squares of the roots:\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=(r+s)^2-2rs\n\\]\n\nSubstitute:\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2-2(-3)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+\\frac{54}{9}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{70}{9}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\frac{70}{9}\\).",
